= Alexandros E. Tzikas


~~~
{}{img_left}{assets/tzikas_chatgpt.png}{Alexandros E. Tzikas}{220px}{}{}
I am a PhD candidate in [https://sisl.stanford.edu SISL] at Stanford University. I am advised by [https://mykel.kochenderfer.com Mykel Kochenderfer] 
and I also work with [https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/ Stephen Boyd].

I am also fortunate to have collaborated with [https://candes.su.domains Emmanuel Candès], [https://hastie.su.domains Trevor Hastie],
and [https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/ Stephen Boyd] in my role as a quantitative researcher at the [https://www.blackrock.com/corporate/ai BlackRock Palo Alto AI Lab]. 

I completed my undergraduate studies in electrical engineering at the Aristotle University of Thessaloniki, with an emphasis on signal processing, communications, and 
information theory.
~~~

== Research interests
  I am generally interested in theory and applications at the intersection of (convex) optimization, statistics, and sequential decision-making under uncertainty. 
  I enjoy building practical methods for problems in quantitative finance, state estimation, and control that are grounded
  in first principles and theoretical insights.
